  "ONE substrate (f4wA). The cutwA leg is DEFERRED to L238 on purpose, which owns the two-substrate first-hop IDENTITY comparison nonselectively with BH-FDR; doing it here would double-bank it.",
  "ONE null family (the l169c degree-neutral destination swaps) -- L207's cross-null law: a deficit/narrowness magnitude is null-specific and does not transport between comparison sets.",
  "The null relocates the CARRIER's destinations only, so it is not a null for any other actor: the 35-actor census is a DESCRIPTIVE cohort read, and its only job is the demotion check, not an effect size.",
  "The carrier's out-weight Gini and L219's Spearman(w_e, u1[t_e]) are DESCRIPTION here (observed while scoping, PREREG 0b.3 / section 5).",
  "Metric 3 keeps T_L fixed and changes only path SELECTION; metric 2 changes both. So an agreement across all three is evidence about the length metric's domain choice, not about the transition law in general.",
